{"name":"Alajuela Toad","hex":"#ffae52","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"toad","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An amphibian, a kind of frog (broad sense, order Anura) with shorter hindlegs and a drier, wartier skin, many in family Bufonidae.","A contemptible or unpleasant person."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To expel (a user) permanently from a MUD or similar system, so that their account is deleted."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/toad"}],"entries":[{"title":"Golden toad","blocks":[{"text":"The golden toad is an extinct species of true toad that was once abundant in a small, high-altitude region of about 4 square kilometres (1.5 mi2) in an area north of the city of Monteverde, Costa Rica. It was endemic to elfin cloud forest. Also called the Monte Verde toad, Alajuela toad and orange toad, it is commonly considered the \"poster child\" for the amphibian decline crisis. This toad was first described in 1966 by herpetologist Jay Savage. The last sighting of a single male golden toad was on 15 May 1989, and it has since been classified as extinct by the International Union for Conservation of Nature (IUCN). The golden toad was declared extinct by the IUCN Red List in 2004."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Bufo_periglenes2.jpg/330px-Bufo_periglenes2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Golden_toad","wikidata":"Q320632"},{"title":"Alajuela","blocks":[{"text":"Alajuela is a district in the Alajuela canton of the Alajuela Province of Costa Rica. As the seat of the Municipality of Alajuela canton, it is awarded the status of city. By virtue of being the city of the first canton of the province, it is also the capital of the Province of Alajuela."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Alajuela%2C_Costa_Rica_-_Night_Skyline.png/330px-Alajuela%2C_Costa_Rica_-_Night_Skyline.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alajuela","wikidata":"Q37104"},{"title":"Toad","blocks":[{"text":"Toad is a generic common name for certain groups of frogs, especially those of the family Bufonidae, that are characterized by short legs and dry, leathery skin with large bumps made of the parotoid glands."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Bombina_bombina_1_%28Marek_Szczepanek%29.jpg/330px-Bombina_bombina_1_%28Marek_Szczepanek%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Toad","wikidata":"Q6453151"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Monte_verde.jpg/500px-Monte_verde.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Monte_verde.jpg/500px-Monte_verde.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Monteverde Cloud Forest Reserve, the golden toad's previous habitat","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMonte_verde.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/La_Iglesia_Central_de_Alajuela.jpg/500px-La_Iglesia_Central_de_Alajuela.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/La_Iglesia_Central_de_Alajuela.jpg/1280px-La_Iglesia_Central_de_Alajuela.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/La_Iglesia_Central_de_Alajuela.jpg/500px-La_Iglesia_Central_de_Alajuela.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALa_Iglesia_Central_de_Alajuela.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Juan_Santamaria_1.J